o":97},{"t":677.271471,"tempo":91},{"t":679.908834,"tempo":78}],"chapters":[{"bar":1,"title":"Orchestral exposition","description":"The violins call across a rising sixth. Bassoon and flute answer before the soloist enters."},{"bar":41,"title":"Solo exposition","description":"The clarinet claims the opening in the middle register; the answering phrase passes briefly to the violins."},{"bar":73,"title":"Second subject in E","description":"A longer-breathed subject begins on the fifth and folds inward. The clarinet elaborates its cadence."},{"bar":105,"title":"Development: broken crossings","description":"In F-sharp minor the sixth splits into unanswered calls. The clarinet meets bassoon, flute and viola in smaller combinations."},{"bar":145,"title":"Dominant and return","description":"The bass stays on E while fragments gather. The return begins in the strings, then yields to the soloist."},{"bar":185,"title":"Second subject at home","description":"The E-major melody now speaks in A. A passage through the minor subdominant darkens its second half."},{"bar":201,"title":"Closing ritornello","description":"Solo passagework gives way to a public orchestral cadence; the dominant is left open."},{"bar":233,"title":"Cadenza","description":"Two unaccompanied paragraphs: the call, an arpeggiated retreat and a winding ascent back to E."},{"bar":249,"title":"Coda","description":"Clarinet and violins share the closing statement. The orchestra answers with firm, short tonic strokes."}]},{"title":"II. Adagio cantabile","subtitle":"The lamp on the far bank","meter":[3,4],"seconds":509.485356,"bars":[{"t":0,"tempo":51},{"t":3.529412,"tempo":50},{"t":7.129412,"tempo":52},{"t":10.59095,"tempo":49},{"t":14.26442,"tempo":51},{"t":17.793831,"tempo":52},{"t":21.25537,"tempo":50},{"t":24.85537,"tempo":48},{"t":28.60537,"tempo":52},{"t":32.066908,"tempo":51},{"t":35.59632,"tempo":53},{"t":38.992546,"tempo":50},{"t":42.592546,"tempo":52},{"t":46.054085,"tempo":53},{"t":49.450311,"tempo":51},